== Transportation ==
{{Main|Transportation in Akyatan}}
[[File:Akyatan Metro.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The [[Akyatan Metro]] rapid transit system serves over 2.8 million passengers daily across seven lines.]]
Akyatan serves as Dagit's primary transportation hub, with extensive air, sea, and land connections to domestic and international destinations. The city's transportation infrastructure has undergone significant modernization since the 1990s, including the development of a comprehensive rapid transit system, expansion of airport facilities, and integration of smart traffic management systems.

=== Air ===
[[Akyatan International Airport]] (AKT) is the primary international gateway to Dagit, handling approximately 22.4 million passengers in 2024. The airport serves as the main hub for [[Dagit Airways]] and offers direct flights to over 45 destinations across Fosia, Illypnia, and Lurandia, including daily services to [[Okami]], [[Toyozawa]], [[Merced]], [[Yomitan]], [[Jingdao]], and [[Miyagami]]. The airport's modern Terminal 3, completed in 2018, features extensive retail and dining facilities, business lounges, and integrated rail connections to the city center.

A second facility, [[Akyatan-Silay International Airport]] (AKS), primarily serves domestic routes and regional connections within the Dagit archipelago. The airport handled 8.2 million passengers in 2024 and provides a hub for budget carriers including [[Airmomo]] and [[Push Air]]. A third facility, the [[Dagumnan City Airport]], serves general aviation and cargo operations.

=== Sea ===
The [[Port of Akyatan]] is Dagit's largest and busiest port, comprising multiple specialized terminals for cargo, passengers, and fishing vessels spread across a natural harbor protected by the Kabisayaan Peninsula. The port handles approximately 65% of Dagit's international maritime trade by volume and serves as a critical transshipment hub for the Shendan Ocean region.

The port offers regular ferry services to major islands throughout the Dagit archipelago through the [[Akyatan Domestic Ferry Terminal]], which handles approximately 14.5 million passengers annually. The [[Akyatan International Ferry Terminal]] provides connections to [[Okaiken]] (via [[Shinagawa]] and [[Tokuyama]]), [[Yanbaru]] (via [[Yomitan]]), [[Kingdom of Zong|Zong]] (via [[Jingdao]]), and [[Nakamizu]] (via [[Miyagami]]). High-speed catamaran services connect Akyatan to [[Yomitan]] in under 4 hours, making it a popular route for both business and leisure travelers.

The [[Akyatan Fish Port Complex]] in the Dagumnan district is one of the largest fish landing and processing facilities in western Fosia, handling approximately 280,000 metric tons of seafood annually. The complex includes ice plants, cold storage facilities, and a fish cannery serving export markets.

=== Land ===
==== Akyatan Metro ====
{{Main|Akyatan Metro}}
The [[Akyatan Metro]] is a [[rapid transit]] system consisting of seven lines operated by the [[Akyatan Metropolitan Transit Authority]] (AMTA), a government-owned corporation under the [[Ministry of Transportation and Communications (Dagit)|Ministry of Transportation and Communications]]. The system serves as the backbone of public transportation within the metropolitan area, carrying over 2.8 million passengers daily across 186 stations and 198 kilometers of operational track.

